## Workflow Demonstrated

```
WEEKLY REVIEW RITUAL

1. 📥 Clear inbox to zero
        ↓
2. 📋 Review all #🔄active notes
        ↓
3. ⏳ Check #⏳waiting items
        ↓
4. 🌱 Evaluate note maturity
        ↓
5. ⬆️ Promote ready notes
        ↓
6. 🔗 Look for new connections
        ↓
7. 📝 Create weekly note
        ↓
8. 🎯 Set next week's focus
```

---

## Maturity Progression Guide

```
📤 SEED (Day 1)
   Raw capture, minimal content
   "I had this thought..."
        ↓
🌱 SEEDLING (Day 5)
   Developed content, some connections
   "Here's what I've learned..."
        ↓
🪴 SAPLING (Week 2+)
   Well-structured, multiple links
   "This connects to several ideas..."
        ↓
🌲 EVERGREEN (Month+)
   Stable, frequently referenced
   "This is a core principle I use..."
        ↓
🍓 FRUIT (Ongoing)
   Produces outputs, widely applied
   "This idea shaped my thinking/work..."
```

---

## Weekly Review Template

```markdown
## 🏆 Wins This Week
- What went well?
- What did I create?
- What connections did I make?

## 🔍 Review
- Inbox cleared? ✅/❌
- Active notes reviewed? ✅/❌
- Waiting items checked? ✅/❌

## 🌱 Note Evolution
- Notes promoted: [list]
- Notes needing attention: [list]

## 🎯 Next Week's Focus
- Top 3 priorities

## 💭 Reflections
- What am I learning?
- What patterns am I noticing?
```

---

## Pattern Recognition

> [!important] A Pattern Emerges
>
> During the review, Alex notices something:
>
> - Mycelium Networks → about **connections creating strength**
> - Compound Growth → about **small additions → big results**
> - Dr. Maya's research → about **networks enabling communication**
>
> *"There's a theme here... something about how networks and growth work together..."*
>
> **This observation will become tomorrow's MOC.**

---

## Alex's Reflection

> "The weekly review is where the magic happens. Not in the daily capture, but in the weekly stepping back. That's when I see patterns I missed. That's when notes evolve. It's only 30 minutes, but it transforms everything."

---

## Try It Yourself

> [!example] Exercise: Your First Weekly Review
> 1. Set aside 30 minutes on a consistent day
> 2. Clear your inbox to zero
> 3. Review all notes created this week
> 4. Ask: "Which notes have grown? Which need attention?"
> 5. Promote at least one note's maturity
> 6. Create a weekly note with wins and focus

---

